  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policies and programmes developed and implemented to promote and improve safety and health at work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In St Lucia, the ILO is working with the Department of Labour to establish the National OSH Programme. ILO regional and sub-regional OSH specialists have reviewed the current national OSH policy 2017. The aspiration is to support St Lucia realise the commitments made under that policy, &#xa0;and realise its strategy which is to ensure the OSH policy provide a framework for national-level action to improve OSH;&#xa0; a comprehensive OSH System is comprising the right infrastructure and resource; a profile that aptly captures the national OSH situation and that there is a time bound programme (3 to 5 year plan) that identifies OSH problems, and clearly sets out objectives, targets and indicators, and implementation mechanisms. Relatedly and important, on the ratification side, St Lucia has expressed its intention to ratify the fundamental ILO Convention 187 in June 2025, which will also increase compliance with OSH protocol. All this activity will lead to a safer working environment for all workers in Saint Lucia, reduce pressure on social security systems when there are work injuries/illnesses, reduces presure on employer-liability systems, and support productivity without losing working time to OSH-related accidents, which is good for the whole of society and the economy.</narrative>
  </description>
